      "title": "The Armor of God",
      "reference": "Ephesians 6:10-18",
      "content": "Paul uses Roman soldier imagery to describe spiritual readiness. Each piece of armor corresponds to a spiritual virtue: truth, righteousness, readiness, faith, salvation, the Word, and prayer.",
